From 2090cadb46a116f9909113712c693a1febed12e6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: itsNintu <itsNintu@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 09:23:17 +0700
Subject: [PATCH] screencopy: support cursor_mode METADATA

Advertise and accept the ScreenCast "metadata" cursor mode: frames are
captured without the cursor and its position is attached to every
PipeWire buffer as SPA_META_Cursor, so recorders can draw their own
cursor, smooth it, or zoom to clicks (e.g. Openscreen's editable cursor).

The pointer is followed with ext-image-copy-capture cursor sessions, one
per output, and mapped onto the shared area (output, region or window).
Buffers keep flowing while only the cursor moves.

Hyprland (as of 0.56) reports cursor session positions in logical px
relative to the source's logical box, rather than buffer px relative to
the captured buffer as the protocol specifies; for windows that box
includes decorations. Output sessions in global logical coordinates are
therefore used for every share type, and window shares look the window's
position and size up through Hyprland's IPC. Once Hyprland follows the
spec, window shares can use a toplevel cursor session directly.

No cursor bitmap is sent yet (bitmap_offset = 0).

Refs: #444
